el will recognize that  seattle is a city  and today is a date  for this we apply feature extractors to  extract  turn-level and dialog level features and  pass them through context encoders  we also extract catalog features based  on the domain and specific catalogs  provided by the developer  we then concatenate the feature  representations  to obtain the final dialog  representation  and con and concatenate it with word  embedding of each token  and use it as input to the model  for the final model we use birth with a  biolistim  architecture the second model  that we use is the action prediction  model or ap  the action prediction model predicts  what action  alexa should take next using the current  user utterance  and also taking into account the whole  dialogue history so far  so in this case after the user says  seattle today  the action prediction model looks at  this input  and the whole conversation and predicts  the best action to take next  is to confirm what the user just said  the action prediction model evaluates  different alternative possible adnex  actions for this we pass the dialog  encoding that i mentioned in the  previous slide  through an mlp and we utilize  endless action hypotheses using a simple  binning strategy  and reject actions in the low confidence  bin  and finally  the last model we have argument filling  this model plus in the values of api and  response template arguments  by looking at the whole dialog context  so far  it does this by picking a slot values  from all the compatible slots that the  ner model recognized earlier  so in this example when the user said  seattle today the ner model  already recognized seattle as a city and  today as a date  and the action prediction model already  decided  that the best thing to do is to confirm  so the argument filling model now goes  ahead  and selects the value seattle as the  input value for the city argument of the  confirm template  and the value today as the input for the  data